---
/**
 * Terms of Use.
 *
 * Written against what the site actually does today. Version 1.0 stated that
 * there was no account and no sign-in; accounts shipped, so sections 3 and 4
 * exist and that claim is gone. A term describing a capability the site does
 * not have is as much a defect as a missing one — when the site gains or loses
 * something, this page changes with it, under a new version and date.
 *
 * The licence section is the one place this has to be exact, and it follows
 * ATTRIBUTION.md rather than asserting a blanket claim: one of the three plates
 * is share-alike, which obliges us as much as it obliges anyone downstream.
 */
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';

const TERMS_VERSION = '2.0';
const LAST_UPDATED = '9 September 2026';
---

<Doc
	title="Terms of Use — The Itti Foundation"
	description="The terms on which The Itti Foundation offers this site: eligibility, accounts, acceptable use, intellectual property and liability."
	eyebrow="Terms of Use"
	heading="Terms of Use"
	lede="The terms on which this site is offered, what you may do with what is on it, and the limits of what it claims to be."
	version={TERMS_VERSION}
	updated={LAST_UPDATED}
>
	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">1. Who we are, and your acceptance</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				This site is operated by <strong>Itti&rsquo;s Skill School Foundation</strong>, a
				Section 8 not-for-profit company incorporated in India and operating as The Itti
				Foundation. In these terms <em>we</em> and <em>us</em> mean the Foundation, and{' '}
				<em>you</em> means the person using the site.
			</p>
			<p>
				By using this site you accept these terms. If you do not accept them, please do
				not use the site. Your use of personal data is governed additionally by our{' '}
				<a class="doc__link" href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, which forms part of these
				terms.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">2. Registration</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				Registration is optional. It records your interest and how we may contact you. It
				does not create a membership, an employment or volunteering relationship, an
				entitlement to any service, or any other contract between us.
			</p>
			<p>When you register you undertake that:</p>
			<dl class="doc__list">
				<dt>The details are accurate</dt>
				<dd>
					And that you will correct them if they cease to be. Your account page allows
					this at any time.
				</dd>
				<dt>They are yours to give</dt>
				<dd>
					If you register on another person&rsquo;s behalf, you confirm that they are
					aware of it and have asked you to.
				</dd>
				<dt>A minor has a guardian</dt>
				<dd>
					A person under eighteen may register only with a parent or lawful guardian
					named. We write to the guardian and do not act on the registration until they
					agree. This requirement is enforced by the registry and cannot be waived.
				</dd>
			</dl>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">3. Accounts and sign-in</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				If you registered with an email address, you may sign in to view and amend the
				record we hold about you.
			</p>
			<dl class="doc__list">
				<dt>There is no password</dt>
				<dd>
					You sign in by requesting a single-use link sent to your registered email
					address. Anyone with access to that mailbox can sign in as you, so keep it
					secure and tell us promptly if you believe it has been compromised.
				</dd>
				<dt>The account is personal to you</dt>
				<dd>
					Do not share access, and do not attempt to reach another person&rsquo;s record.
				</dd>
				<dt>You may close it</dt>
				<dd>
					Write to us and we will erase your record, subject to the retention set out in
					the Privacy Policy.
				</dd>
			</dl>
			<p>
				We take reasonable care to keep the sign-in mechanism secure, but you are
				responsible for activity carried out through your account where it results from
				your own act or omission.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">4. Content you provide</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				Your account allows you to add a short biography and links to your own profiles or
				addresses. You remain the owner of what you write. You grant us only the permission
				necessary to store it and display it back to you.
			</p>
			<p>You are responsible for it, and you undertake not to submit:</p>
			<dl class="doc__list">
				<dt>Another person&rsquo;s material or identity</dt>
				<dd>
					Including links to accounts that are not yours, or content that infringes
					someone else&rsquo;s rights.
				</dd>
				<dt>Unlawful or abusive content</dt>
				<dd>
					Anything defamatory, obscene, harassing, or prohibited by Indian law.
				</dd>
				<dt>Other people&rsquo;s personal data</dt>
				<dd>Beyond the guardian details the registration asks for.</dd>
			</dl>
			<p>
				Links you add are self-asserted: we do not verify that an account belongs to you
				and displaying one is not an endorsement of it. We may remove content that
				breaches these terms, and will tell you when we do.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">5. Acceptable use</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				You may read, quote, link to, print and share the material on this site freely,
				subject to section 7. You may not:
			</p>
			<dl class="doc__list">
				<dt>Interfere with the site</dt>
				<dd>
					By probing it, overloading it, circumventing its security, or attempting to
					reach any part of the system not offered to you.
				</dd>
				<dt>Submit false or unauthorised details</dt>
				<dd>Including registering a person who has not asked you to.</dd>
				<dt>Extract the site at scale</dt>
				<dd>
					Automated collection that imposes a material load on our infrastructure, or
					that reproduces the site rather than reading it.
				</dd>
				<dt>Misrepresent your relationship with us</dt>
				<dd>
					By using our name, marks or wording in a way that suggests we said something we
					did not, or that you speak for the Foundation.
				</dd>
			</dl>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">6. No professional advice</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				This site discusses neurodivergence, cancer, mental health and the environment.
				Nothing on it constitutes medical, psychological, legal or financial advice, a
				diagnosis, or a treatment plan, and nothing on it establishes a
				practitioner&ndash;patient relationship.
			</p>
			<p>
				It is not a substitute for a qualified professional who knows your circumstances,
				and it should never be the reason you start, stop or change any aspect of your
				care. <strong
					>We are not a crisis service. If you are in immediate danger, contact your local
					emergency services.</strong
				>
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">7. Intellectual property</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				This site incorporates work under several different licences. The complete record
				travels with the source code in <code>ATTRIBUTION.md</code>; the following is a
				summary.
			</p>
			<dl class="doc__list">
				<dt>The heron</dt>
				<dd>
					<em>Hummingbird at Arizona-Sonora Desert Museum</em> (2023) by Lorie Shaull,
					under{' '}
					<a
						class="doc__link"
						href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"
						rel="noopener">CC BY-SA 4.0</a
					>, colour-graded and resized by us. Because that licence is share-alike, our
					version is offered under the same terms and any derivative must carry the same
					notice. This obligation binds us as it binds you.
				</dd>
				<dt>The Cajal and the Bourgery</dt>
				<dd>
					<em>Purkinje cell of the cerebellum</em> (1899) by Santiago Ram&oacute;n y
					Cajal, and Plate 42 of the{' '}
					<em>Trait&eacute; complet de l&rsquo;anatomie de l&rsquo;homme</em>{' '}
					(1831&ndash;54), drawn by Nicolas-Henri Jacob for J. M. Bourgery. Both are in
					the public domain. We graded them; the originals belong to everyone.
				</dd>
				<dt>The typefaces</dt>
				<dd>Each under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, and self-hosted.</dd>
				<dt>Everything else</dt>
				<dd>
					Our name, our mark, the project marks, the photography and the text are the
					Foundation&rsquo;s and are not licensed for reuse. Please write to us if you
					wish to use them.
				</dd>
			</dl>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">8. Third-party links</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				Where we link to another organisation we are directing you, not endorsing them. We
				do not control those sites and are not responsible for their content, their
				availability, or what they do with your data. Their own terms and privacy notices
				apply once you leave this site.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">9. Availability and disclaimers</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				The site is provided on an &ldquo;as is&rdquo; and &ldquo;as available&rdquo;
				basis. We do not warrant that it will be uninterrupted or error-free, that every
				page is current, or that it is fit for any particular purpose of yours. We may
				modify, suspend or withdraw any part of it without notice.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">10. Limitation of liability</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for indirect or consequential
				loss, or for loss of data, profit or goodwill, arising from your use of this site.
			</p>
			<p>
				Nothing in these terms excludes or limits liability that cannot lawfully be
				excluded or limited, including liability for death or personal injury caused by
				negligence or for fraud; and nothing in them removes a right you have under Indian
				consumer or data protection law.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">11. Suspension</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				We may suspend or withdraw access, or remove a registration or account, where these
				terms are breached or where required by law. Where we do so we will tell you, and
				where the breach can be remedied we will say how.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">12. Changes to these terms</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				These terms carry a version number and a date, shown at the head of this page. When
				they change materially, both change. We do not edit a live document and leave its
				date untouched. Continued use of the site after a change constitutes acceptance of
				the revised terms.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">13. Governing law</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				These terms are governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of India,
				and any dispute arising from them is subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the
				courts having jurisdiction over the Foundation&rsquo;s registered office.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="doc__section">
		<h2 class="doc__h">14. Contact</h2>
		<div class="doc__body">
			<p>
				Questions about these terms or about this site:{' '}
				<a class="doc__link" href="mailto:hello@itti.org.in">hello@itti.org.in</a>. We
				respond within five working days.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</Doc>
